Today is Wednesday.
I say goodbye to Anitha.
I walk to the bicycle shop.
I reach there at exactly seven o'clock.
The mechanic is in the shop.
He finishes the work on my bicycle.
"The cycle is ready now," he says to me.
I say thank you to him.
My bicycle looks like new.
I feel very happy.
I ride the bicycle to the apartment.
I go to the office every day.
I always go to the office by bus.
But from now on, sometimes I will ride the bicycle.
